./logs/iter_003_solution_gate.stdout.log:5:But the critic identified serious unresolved gaps. Most importantly, the solver mixes an instance-wise counterexample, a sufficiency theorem, and a sketched universal/minimax lower bound without fixing the quantifier regime. The concatenated block lower bound is not proved; only the finite \(0^N c\) gadget is accepted. Therefore this is not yet a complete characterization or replacement theorem.
./logs/iter_003_solution_gate.stdout.log:11:- regret should use \(\sup_a\), not \(\max_a\), unless attainment is proved;
./logs/iter_003_solution_gate.stdout.log:13:- any necessity statement must specify process-aware vs universal/minimax vs horizon-aware learners.
