./logs/iter_009_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:3945:./logs/iter_008_synthesis.stderr.log:9524:working_notes/counterexamples.md:163:if the learner is told the evaluation horizon \(T_j=M+N+j\), it can tailor its zero-block quotes to \(c_j\). The common zero-block action law across \(j\), which is the input to the \(\kappa(C)\) averaging argument, is then absent. This is the same obstruction as the horizon/process-aware oracle collapse: CL-026 and CL-027 apply only to one infinite horizon-oblivious policy.
