./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:707:Failed or strongly weakened. Predictable sparse spikes can make \(\Delta_T(H_T)=\Omega(T)\) along infinitely many horizons for every \(H_T\log T=o(T)\), while a process-aware learner posts a known near-optimal quote and gets sublinear regret. Raw delayed reward mass is not the same as information needed for learning.
./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:709:## FA-004: Using Comparator `max` Without Checking Attainment
./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:743:- Lancewicki, Segal, Koren, and Mansour (ICML/PMLR 2021) studies stochastic bandits with unrestricted and infinite delays, with quantile-based delay dependence. Verified source; relevant for quantile alternatives to uniform tails.
./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:785:If a future public price is deterministically \(c\in(0,1]\), then quotes \(a<c\) trade while \(a\ge c\) do not. The fixed-action payoff approaches the value at \(c\) as \(a\uparrow c\) but is not attained at \(a=c\). Thus the problem should use \(\sup_a\) or add conditions ensuring a maximum exists.
./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:832:- Tal Lancewicki, Shahar Segal, Tomer Koren, Yishay Mansour. "Stochastic Multi-Armed Bandits with Unrestricted Delay Distributions." ICML 2021, PMLR 139:5969-5978. https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/lancewicki21a.html. Relevance: quantile-style control under unbounded or infinite delays.
