./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1059:- Lancewicki, Segal, Koren, and Mansour (ICML/PMLR 2021) studies stochastic bandits with unrestricted and infinite delays, with quantile-based delay dependence. Verified source; relevant for quantile alternatives to uniform tails.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1069:- Duetting, Guruganesh, Schneider, and Wang (ICML/PMLR 2023) is now verified. It studies one-sided Lipschitz maximization, motivated by pricing/contract design, and gives very small regret in that setting. Potential tool for threshold reward geometry and improved discretization, but delayed/adversarial time variation may block direct application.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1072:## Quantifiers, Universal Regret, And Minimax
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1074:- Cesa-Bianchi and Lugosi, *Prediction, Learning, and Games* (Cambridge University Press, 2006), verified from the authors' official book page. It is useful for standard online-learning quantifiers: algorithms working for all individual sequences relative to a reference class, expert advice, and minimax regret.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1076:- Cesa-Bianchi, Gentile, Mansour, and Minora (COLT/PMLR 2016) is now verified. The source explicitly mentions a minimax characterization for bandit learning with delay as a by-product. Relevant lower-bound methodology/background for class-uniform delayed-feedback impossibility, not direct support for the market-making conjecture.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1085:Existing delayed-learning literature supports sufficiency via bounded, total, adaptive, optimistic, or skipped delay terms. It does not support necessity of the unweighted \(\beta\) tail. Standard online-learning references also reinforce that the meaningful lower-bound regime is usually universal or minimax, not horizon- and law-specific oracle policies. The literature is more aligned with aggregate, quantile, best-arm, skipped, value-of-information, or horizon-censored delay quantities, but the iteration's counterexamples show even raw delayed reward mass is not necessary for instance-wise learnability unless tied to unpredictability or information acquisition.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1109:If a future public price is deterministically \(c\in(0,1]\), then quotes \(a<c\) trade while \(a\ge c\) do not. The fixed-action payoff approaches the value at \(c\) as \(a\uparrow c\) but is not attained at \(a=c\). Thus the problem should use \(\sup_a\) or add conditions ensuring a maximum exists.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1162:This supports universal-class/minimax lower bounds after concatenating dominant blocks \(0^{N_i}c_i\), but it does not refute instance-wise learnability by a learner that knows the deterministic continuation sequence.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1168:If the terminal bit \(c\in\{1/2,1\}\) is drawn randomly and the regret remains \(\sup_a\mathbb E[\text{fixed-action reward}]-\mathbb E[\text{learner reward}]\), the stochastic instance can be easy: the learner can target the best fixed quote in expectation. Thus the two-continuation construction should be used as an adversarial deterministic class or minimax/Yao lower-bound device, not as a hard stochastic process without changing the regret notion.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1193:- minimax lower bound over processes failing a condition;
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1208:Candidate formal objects: conditional value-of-information gaps, Le Cam/two-continuation moduli, or argmax-stability gaps for \(\sup_a V_T(a)\). Avoid tautological quantities unless they produce an algorithm or a clean lower bound.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1222:Exploit \(r_t(a)=a\,1\{\max_{s>t}P_s>a\}\). Prices reveal nested threshold information across quotes. Possible payoffs: improved discretization, adaptive grids, or one-sided Lipschitz methods. Keep this separate from delay-tail characterization until the basic theorem is settled.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1239:Refuted/weakened: \(\beta\)-necessity, \(\gamma\)-necessity, and \(\Delta_T\)-necessity all fail or are unproved for process-aware instance-level learnability. Comparator `max` is also unsafe under strict crossing; use `sup`.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1259:- The comparator `max` is unsafe under strict crossing and atoms; future statements should use `sup` or prove attainment.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1284:- Formalize the concatenated deterministic block-class lower bound with dominant lengths \(M_i=o(N_i)\), careful cross-block reward accounting, and explicit universal/minimax quantifiers.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1285:- Develop a decision-relevant delayed-tail quantity based on indistinguishable continuations, conditional value of information, or argmax stability.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1290:- The two-continuation construction should not be presented as a hard stochastic mixture under the current regret definition; it is a deterministic-class/minimax lower-bound gadget.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1295:- Updated the literature map to distinguish direct delayed full-information support from adaptive bandit/OCO, threshold-geometry, and minimax-background references.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1325:- The block lower bound is universal/minimax, not instance-wise.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1354:- Tal Lancewicki, Shahar Segal, Tomer Koren, Yishay Mansour. "Stochastic Multi-Armed Bandits with Unrestricted Delay Distributions." ICML 2021, PMLR 139:5969-5978. https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/lancewicki21a.html. Relevance: quantile-style control under unbounded or infinite delays.
./logs/iter_003_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1376:- Nicolo Cesa-Bianchi, Claudio Gentile, Yishay Mansour, Alberto Minora. "Delay and Cooperation in Nonstochastic Bandits." 29th Annual Conference on Learning Theory, PMLR 49:605-622, 2016. https://proceedings.mlr.press/v49/cesa-bianchi16.html. Relevance: delayed-bandit minimax background and lower-bound methodology for class-uniform readings.
