./logs/iter_010_solution_gate.stderr.log:3105:- The monotone-threshold derandomization lemma is credible. For fixed grid-valued monotone \(d_1\ge\cdots\ge d_n\), Hoeffding applies to independent bounded variables
./logs/iter_010_solution_gate.stderr.log:3109:  The number of grid-valued monotone paths is \(\binom{n+m}{m}\), so a union bound is subexponential for \(m=o(n)\).
